WEBVTT

00:02.308 --> 00:03.900
&lt;i>Previously on Two and a Half Men:&lt;/i>

00:04.077 --> 00:07.706
- So how's Charlie doing?
- Oh, he's fine. Actually, he's engaged.

00:07.881 --> 00:10.543
You told her I was engaged?
Why would you do that?

00:10.717 --> 00:13.015
Charlie, there's a woman named Mia
on the phone.

00:14.220 --> 00:15.949
I'll take it.

00:16.556 --> 00:18.353
Hi, Charlie.

00:20.527 --> 00:22.085
Mia.

00:25.398 --> 00:29.357
- So how are you?
- Great. How are you?

00:29.536 --> 00:32.198
- Fine, fine.
- Still engaged.

00:34.607 --> 00:36.199
Come, sit, join us.

00:36.376 --> 00:39.504
- Are you sure I'm not interrupting?
- No, no, of course not.

00:39.679 --> 00:41.704
Yeah, his fiancée just left.

00:42.749 --> 00:45.775
- Sorry I missed her.
- She's in the parking lot. I'll get her.

00:46.419 --> 00:50.287
So, what's going on with you these days?
You still dancing?

00:50.490 --> 00:52.424
I'm a little old for ballet now.

00:52.592 --> 00:54.787
Oh, that can't be right.
You look great.

00:54.994 --> 00:58.623
Young and vibrant and taut.

01:00.366 --> 01:03.199
You know who else has a great body?
Charlie's fiancée.

01:03.369 --> 01:05.701
In fact,
Charlie calls her "boobalicious."

01:07.507 --> 01:09.600
I'm really happy you found somebody.

01:09.776 --> 01:11.971
Thank you. She's great.
Really, really great.

01:12.145 --> 01:13.442
Boobalicious.

01:16.115 --> 01:18.106
If you're not dancing,
what are you up to?

01:18.284 --> 01:20.548
I'm trying for a singing career.

01:20.720 --> 01:22.312
No kidding. That's terrific.

01:22.522 --> 01:25.719
- You know who's a wonderful singer?
- Charlie's fiancée?

01:25.892 --> 01:28.884
Actually I was gonna say
Ms. Celine Dion.

01:30.163 --> 01:32.154
I have no idea about Chelsea.

01:32.332 --> 01:35.096
Although she does have
a set of lungs on her.

01:35.935 --> 01:37.095
Right.

01:37.270 --> 01:39.636
Listen, I'm putting together
a demo of some songs.

01:39.806 --> 01:43.139
Any chance you could help me
with arrangements, maybe play piano?

01:43.443 --> 01:45.968
Oh, wow. That sounds like fun.

01:46.145 --> 01:50.639
It's just, you know,
kind of awkward because, you know...

01:50.817 --> 01:52.079
He's getting married.

01:54.954 --> 01:56.945
- I can find you somebody else.
- Terrific.

01:57.123 --> 02:00.650
- Let me give you my number.
- You still at 696-336-725?

02:00.827 --> 02:02.852
Yeah. I can't believe you remember it.

02:03.062 --> 02:04.927
Well, I have a little memory trick.

02:05.098 --> 02:08.499
You change the numbers to letters,
it spells out "oxofempal."

02:09.602 --> 02:10.933
Oh, good trick.

02:12.805 --> 02:15.433
I should get going.
Wonderful to see you again.

02:15.608 --> 02:17.200
Same here.

02:17.377 --> 02:18.935
- You too, Alan.
- Bye-bye.

02:21.981 --> 02:24.211
- Charlie?
- Yeah.

02:24.817 --> 02:26.079
I've missed you.

02:36.362 --> 02:38.023
"Oxofempal"?

02:42.201 --> 02:44.829
Hot! Hot! Hot! Aah!

02:47.707 --> 02:49.538
You have to dial 1 first.

03:02.188 --> 03:04.952
Hey, Berta,
what do you know about Percocet?

03:05.725 --> 03:07.920
Three of them
with a Mickey's Big Mouth...

03:08.094 --> 03:11.359
...can make you run buck-naked
through a Taco Bell.

03:12.165 --> 03:13.359
Why do you ask?

03:13.533 --> 03:15.899
Mom says Grandma Lenore
can't hold the new baby...

03:16.069 --> 03:17.627
...until she stops popping them.

03:17.804 --> 03:19.533
That's probably a good idea.

03:19.706 --> 03:23.107
You drop one kid,
you gain a reputation as a kid-dropper.

03:23.910 --> 03:26.140
So how do you like
having a new baby sister?

03:26.312 --> 03:29.475
Well, she eats, she sleeps, she poops.
So far, I'm not impressed.

03:30.983 --> 03:33.781
Give her a bad haircut
and she'd be you.

03:34.420 --> 03:37.446
Excuse me,
but I paid 9 bucks for this haircut.

03:38.391 --> 03:39.585
Sorry.

03:40.326 --> 03:42.817
Besides, the baby doesn't look
anything like me.

03:42.995 --> 03:46.123
In fact, she doesn't look
like my mom or my stepdad, either.

03:46.299 --> 03:47.596
Who does she look like?

03:48.101 --> 03:51.593
Kind of like
a girl version of my dad.

03:52.638 --> 03:56.096
I thought your dad
was the girl version of your dad.

03:57.610 --> 04:01.068
I'm telling you, Charlie,
this is a bad idea.

04:01.247 --> 04:04.182
What's the big deal?
I'm just gonna find her a piano player.

04:04.350 --> 04:05.908
I saw the way you looked at her.

04:06.085 --> 04:08.417
You say piano player,
but you mean organist.

04:09.355 --> 04:11.482
That's ridiculous.
I'm engaged to Chelsea.

04:11.657 --> 04:14.023
I'm living with Chelsea.
I'm in love with Chelsea.

04:14.227 --> 04:16.855
- What's Chelsea's phone number?
- What?

04:17.029 --> 04:19.463
What does it spell?
Your little memory trick.

04:19.632 --> 04:21.429
Oh, uh...

04:21.601 --> 04:25.298
It's "jklpuzo."

04:25.805 --> 04:29.138
Really? Okay, let's test it out.

04:29.308 --> 04:32.368
Is that 818-JKLPUZO...

04:32.545 --> 04:35.810
...or 310-JKLPUZO?

04:35.982 --> 04:37.176
All right, I made it up.

04:37.350 --> 04:39.511
I don't have to call Chelsea,
she lives here.

04:39.685 --> 04:41.448
You don't have to call Mia, either.

04:41.621 --> 04:44.146
Oh, yeah?
Well, what about you and Melissa?

04:44.323 --> 04:45.347
What does that
have to do with anything?

04:45.525 --> 04:48.255
Nothing. I'm changing the subject
to your peccadilloes.

04:49.662 --> 04:52.028
You were banging Melissa
in the storage closet...

04:52.198 --> 04:54.063
...while your ex-wife was giving birth.

04:54.267 --> 04:57.759
- We don't know she's my daughter.
Who's your daughter?

05:00.273 --> 05:03.174
You're my daughter, I'm your daughter...

05:03.342 --> 05:06.311
...this whole court is out of daughter!

05:08.681 --> 05:11.616
Al Pacino. It's a great movie.

05:13.152 --> 05:14.551
Hoo-ah!

05:15.888 --> 05:17.150
See that one?

05:20.893 --> 05:22.019
That was close.

05:22.428 --> 05:23.554
Good thing he's slow.

05:23.729 --> 05:27.062
Yeah, well, Judith's mom dropped him
when he was a baby.

05:34.674 --> 05:36.073
Wow.

05:37.076 --> 05:38.805
Yeah.

05:40.112 --> 05:42.376
What brought that on?

05:43.449 --> 05:46.077
You're the one
who started talking dirty.

05:47.520 --> 05:49.750
All I said was, "What'd you do today?"

05:49.922 --> 05:52.516
There you go again, you nasty girl.

05:53.259 --> 05:55.284
Okay, seriously.

05:55.461 --> 05:56.826
What did you do today?

05:58.831 --> 06:02.062
Nothing. Just a regular day.

06:02.235 --> 06:04.863
Had coffee with you,
hung out with Alan a little bit...

06:05.037 --> 06:07.631
...then came home, had a drink,
took a nap...

06:07.840 --> 06:11.435
...next thing I know you're walking
in the front door with your whore talk.

06:11.611 --> 06:13.442
All right, whatever.

06:13.980 --> 06:17.108
- Oh, yeah, there was one other thing.
- Really.

06:18.584 --> 06:20.643
Yeah. I ran into an old buddy.

06:20.853 --> 06:24.482
- What's her name?
- Her? Why do you assume it's a her?

06:25.291 --> 06:29.728
When you've seen your old guy friends,
you don't try to hump me into a coma.

06:30.796 --> 06:33.128
Fair point. It was Mia.

06:34.233 --> 06:37.725
- Mia, the old buddy you almost married?
- Yeah.

06:40.072 --> 06:42.597
- And?
- And nothing.

06:44.443 --> 06:47.776
She did ask me if I'd help her out
with this music thing she's doing.

06:47.947 --> 06:49.642
- But I said no.
- How come?

06:50.249 --> 06:52.149
I thought it'd be inappropriate.

06:52.318 --> 06:56.652
- Why? You still have feelings for her?
- No, no, of course not.

06:56.822 --> 07:00.121
- Then why wouldn't you help her out?
- What?

07:01.193 --> 07:04.651
I mean, if she's just a friend,
then why would it be inappropriate?

07:06.666 --> 07:08.463
Okay.

07:09.502 --> 07:12.266
Uh... No reason.

07:12.438 --> 07:16.670
- So you're saying I should help her out?
- Unless you still have feelings for her.

07:17.843 --> 07:19.174
I guess I'll help her.

07:19.345 --> 07:22.143
- Good.
- Good.

07:24.951 --> 07:26.851
Or bad.

07:29.221 --> 07:31.348
Probably bad.

07:32.959 --> 07:34.927
I'm gonna go with bad.

07:40.199 --> 07:41.632
Hi, Charlie.

07:42.068 --> 07:44.832
We were having a moonlight skinny-dip
in the ocean.

07:45.004 --> 07:46.904
Good thinking.
Nothing more romantic...

07:47.073 --> 07:49.940
...than seaweed hanging
from a cold, shriveled penis.

07:50.843 --> 07:51.867
There's no seaweed.

07:52.044 --> 07:53.534
Oh, my!

07:57.149 --> 08:00.710
- Don't put it on the table!
- Sorry.

08:00.886 --> 08:03.218
Alan, what do you say
we take a hot shower...

08:03.389 --> 08:06.324
...and unshrink the Snuffleupagus?

08:06.492 --> 08:09.655
He'll be fine, it's Bert and Ernie
I'm worried about.

08:09.829 --> 08:13.356
I think Bert has ascended to my rib cage.
Go ahead. I'll be right there.

08:13.532 --> 08:14.897
- Okey-doke.
- Okay.

08:17.837 --> 08:19.236
Hey, can I ask you something?

08:19.405 --> 08:21.999
I am not gonna help you
find your missing testicle.

08:22.475 --> 08:25.342
- No, it's about Melissa.
- What about her?

08:25.511 --> 08:27.570
Now that we're seeing
each other again...

08:27.747 --> 08:30.773
...the fact that she lives with her mom
presents a problem.

08:30.983 --> 08:33.349
Why, because you tickled
Mom's Elmo?

08:34.553 --> 08:38.387
It was just light necking.
I never touched her Elmo.

08:39.191 --> 08:42.854
Anyway, since you've set the precedent
of having girlfriends move in here...

08:43.029 --> 08:45.293
...I was wondering if maybe...
- No.

08:45.998 --> 08:51.026
- Why not? You let Chelsea move in.
- It's my house. You are a guest.

08:51.203 --> 08:54.138
By "guest" I mean
"leech I tolerate until our mother dies...

08:54.306 --> 08:57.639
...and she can't lay a guilt trip on me
for kicking you to the curb."

08:57.810 --> 08:59.402
You're gonna kick me out
when Mom dies?

08:59.578 --> 09:01.773
You're planning on being here
until Mom dies?

09:01.947 --> 09:03.642
Okay, we're getting off-subject.

09:03.816 --> 09:07.718
- What about Jake? You let Jake move in.
- You're not helping your case here.

09:07.887 --> 09:10.321
- But I'm just saying I ca...
- I said, no!

09:14.660 --> 09:17.424
Hm. Hey, Bert, welcome back.

09:29.308 --> 09:31.333
&lt;i>You'll never find&lt;/i>

09:33.012 --> 09:35.310
&lt;i>As long as you live&lt;/i>

09:36.716 --> 09:38.775
&lt;i>Someone who loves you&lt;/i>

09:39.552 --> 09:42.851
&lt;i>Tender like I do&lt;/i>

09:45.891 --> 09:47.916
&lt;i>You'll never find&lt;/i>

09:50.129 --> 09:52.290
&lt;i>No matter where you search&lt;/i>

09:53.632 --> 09:56.157
&lt;i>Someone who cares about you&lt;/i>

09:56.335 --> 09:59.862
&lt;i>The way I do&lt;/i>

10:02.041 --> 10:05.101
&lt;i>Whoa, I'm not braggin' on myself, baby&lt;/i>

10:06.212 --> 10:09.477
&lt;i>'Cause I'm the one who loves you
And there's no one else&lt;/i>

10:10.149 --> 10:14.051
&lt;i>No one else&lt;/i>

10:19.325 --> 10:22.123
That's a pretty mouth,
but it ain't made for singing.

10:22.294 --> 10:24.592
- What's it made for?
- Eating.

10:25.030 --> 10:26.327
Oh.

10:26.499 --> 10:28.160
I thought maybe she meant oral sex.

10:30.569 --> 10:32.332
&lt;i>You're gonna miss my lovin'&lt;/i>

10:32.505 --> 10:38.466
&lt;i>You're gonna miss, miss, miss my love&lt;/i>

10:40.813 --> 10:41.973
So?

10:43.048 --> 10:44.481
Wow.

10:44.850 --> 10:47.318
- You wanna run it again?
- I don't.

10:48.254 --> 10:51.189
I mean, there's a danger
of over-rehearsing it.

10:51.357 --> 10:53.018
Yeah. Plus, I kind of nailed it, right?

10:53.893 --> 10:55.986
I don't see it getting any better.

10:56.495 --> 10:59.692
That is so sweet, Charlie.
Thank you.

10:59.865 --> 11:01.856
I don't know
how I'd do this without you.

11:02.034 --> 11:03.558
Hey, I don't deserve any credit.

11:03.736 --> 11:07.001
God gave you that voice.
I had nothing to do with it.

11:08.507 --> 11:10.634
- Oh, hello.
- Oh, hey, hi.

11:11.911 --> 11:15.005
There she is.
Chelsea, this is Mia. Mia, this is Chelsea.

11:15.181 --> 11:16.580
- Hi.
Hi.

11:16.749 --> 11:19.877
- We were just rehearsing.
- I'm sorry. I didn't mean to interrupt.

11:20.052 --> 11:23.886
What? No, there's nothing to interrupt.
She's singing, and I'm playing piano.

11:24.056 --> 11:27.457
Alan, Berta and Jake are in the kitchen.
Guys, Chelsea's home.

11:27.626 --> 11:29.287
Hey.

11:30.930 --> 11:32.420
- I should get going.
- Good.

11:32.865 --> 11:36.460
I mean, you don't have to, but good.
Rehearsal was good.

11:36.669 --> 11:38.637
You've got yourself a terrific guy here.

11:38.804 --> 11:40.863
- I know. Nice to meet you.
- You too.

11:41.040 --> 11:43.304
- I'll see you Saturday at the studio?
You bet.

11:43.475 --> 11:44.567
&lt;i>You'll never find...&lt;/i>

11:44.743 --> 11:46.870
No, no. Save your voice.

11:51.217 --> 11:52.411
Yikes.

11:52.585 --> 11:53.711
So how'd it go?

11:54.720 --> 11:57.211
Well, um, how can I put this?

11:57.389 --> 12:00.085
She's the picture you stick
on the cover of an album...

12:00.259 --> 12:02.227
...by a fat girl who can actually sing.

12:02.828 --> 12:06.924
That's not what I mean.
Were there any, you know, sparks?

12:07.099 --> 12:09.294
No. No sparks.

12:09.468 --> 12:10.935
Why would there be sparks?

12:11.103 --> 12:13.833
I'm with you. We're engaged.
We're gonna be married.

12:14.006 --> 12:16.839
You and me, that's the sparks...

12:17.209 --> 12:18.437
...baby.

12:20.279 --> 12:23.009
Relax, Charlie, I trust you.

12:27.486 --> 12:30.649
Okay, lady,
you're really starting to piss me off.

12:34.827 --> 12:36.818
Thanks for seeing me
on such short notice.

12:36.996 --> 12:41.194
No problem, Charlie, just as long as
you're willing to pay my weekend rates.

12:41.734 --> 12:43.099
You've got weekend rates?

12:43.269 --> 12:46.033
Yep, and you probably
don't wanna waste time haggling.

12:47.273 --> 12:49.673
Now, what's the big emergency?

12:49.842 --> 12:53.334
Well, you might not think
it's a big emergency, but trust me, it is.

12:53.512 --> 12:54.672
Okay.

12:54.847 --> 12:56.712
I'm really constipated.

12:57.883 --> 13:01.478
You do realize
which end of the body I specialize in.

13:01.921 --> 13:04.048
I know, I know.
I'm not here for an enema.

13:04.223 --> 13:06.350
Good, because that couch
isn't Scotchgarded.

13:07.860 --> 13:09.760
I'm thinking it's psychosomatic...

13:09.929 --> 13:13.729
...because I've tried coffee, fiber,
laxatives...

13:13.899 --> 13:16.800
...and something my housekeeper said
was a suppository...

13:17.002 --> 13:20.028
...but I now suspect
was a practical joke.

13:20.773 --> 13:25.073
All right.
So psychosomatic constipation.

13:25.244 --> 13:27.144
Good name for a rock band, huh?

13:27.313 --> 13:30.111
Weekend rates, Charlie.

13:30.883 --> 13:33.943
What's been going on? How are things
with you and your fiancée?

13:34.119 --> 13:38.283
Great. She lives with me, we're planning
the wedding, couldn't be better.

13:38.457 --> 13:39.924
Good. And how's work?

13:40.392 --> 13:43.657
Well, it's been pretty slow,
but thankfully the house is paid off...

13:43.829 --> 13:46.764
...my pension is funded,
and I've given up prostitutes.

13:46.932 --> 13:50.459
All I need is drinking money.
What's that, a couple grand a month?

13:50.636 --> 13:52.467
That sounds about right.

13:52.905 --> 13:54.896
And, hey, do you remember Mia?

13:55.074 --> 13:56.507
Your ex-fiancée, the dancer?

13:56.675 --> 13:57.835
Wow, you remember.

13:58.043 --> 14:01.069
I'm not sitting here sketching ponies,
Charlie.

14:03.449 --> 14:04.916
Anyway, I ran into her.

14:05.084 --> 14:07.848
- Really? And how'd that go?
- Fine. Fine.

14:08.053 --> 14:11.489
She looks great, she's single again,
told me she missed me.

14:11.657 --> 14:13.625
- Uh-huh.
- I always dig that.

14:15.194 --> 14:18.095
She asked me if I could help her
with this music project...

14:18.263 --> 14:19.662
...and I said no.

14:19.832 --> 14:23.131
But Chelsea said if I didn't have
feelings for her, why not do it...

14:23.302 --> 14:25.702
...so I did it.
- Interesting.

14:25.871 --> 14:28.533
- When did all this happen?
- Three, four day ago.

14:28.707 --> 14:30.800
And how long
have you been constipated?

14:31.844 --> 14:34.074
I don't know, three, four days.

14:35.981 --> 14:37.573
You think there's a connection?

14:38.017 --> 14:40.281
I'm leaning that way.

14:40.653 --> 14:42.848
You obviously still have
feelings for Mia...

14:43.022 --> 14:44.956
...and yet you're committed
to Chelsea.

14:45.124 --> 14:48.525
It's an emotional conflict,
and until you resolve that conflict...

14:48.694 --> 14:51.561
...you're going to be physically blocked.
- English, please.

14:51.730 --> 14:54.460
As soon as you pick one,
you can go two.

14:58.470 --> 15:01.997
- What happens if I can't pick?
- I don't know. C-section?

15:06.679 --> 15:09.580
Anyway, she said
I have to resolve the conflict...

15:09.748 --> 15:13.047
...because my emotions are connected
to my lower intestine.

15:13.652 --> 15:14.846
That makes sense.

15:15.020 --> 15:18.012
You think with your penis
and your head's up your ass.

15:20.325 --> 15:22.259
The baby just kicked.

15:23.362 --> 15:24.386
Baby?

15:24.563 --> 15:28.556
Well, it's not technically a baby,
but we know it's gonna look like you.

15:30.269 --> 15:32.567
- Hey, Charlie.
- Hey.

15:37.443 --> 15:40.776
- What's she still doing here?
- She went away and she came back.

15:40.946 --> 15:44.109
- She's not moving in, Alan.
- Of course not. You said no, it's no.

15:44.283 --> 15:46.751
- We're out of milk. I'll run to the market.
- Okay.

15:50.723 --> 15:52.588
She likes milk.

15:53.158 --> 15:55.285
How are you gonna resolve
your conflict?

15:55.461 --> 15:58.089
I'm not sure.
I may have to sleep with Mia.

15:58.263 --> 15:59.855
What?

16:00.365 --> 16:01.923
Okay, here's the deal.

16:04.303 --> 16:06.396
If I back out of the recording session...

16:06.572 --> 16:09.905
...Chelsea will think I still have feelings.
- All right.

16:10.075 --> 16:13.067
If I spend any more time with Mia
without sleeping with her...

16:13.245 --> 16:16.737
...l'm gonna split like a roasted pistachio
and nobody wants that.

16:17.282 --> 16:20.649
Charlie, cheating on Chelsea
makes absolutely no sense whatsoever.

16:20.819 --> 16:24.255
That's what I thought,
but my shrink was pretty adamant.

16:26.925 --> 16:32.295
Just promise if anything happens to me,
you'll raise it as your own.

16:38.270 --> 16:40.397
&lt;i>Down in Louisiana&lt;/i>

16:41.507 --> 16:44.965
&lt;i>Where the alligators grow so mean&lt;/i>

16:45.711 --> 16:49.147
&lt;i>Lived a girl that I swear to the world&lt;/i>

16:49.314 --> 16:51.976
&lt;i>Made the alligators look tame&lt;/i>

16:52.151 --> 16:53.982
&lt;i>Polk Salad Annie&lt;/i>

16:56.822 --> 16:59.757
I know, I know.
It's hard to believe I'm not banging her.

17:00.959 --> 17:02.950
Then why are we here?

17:03.529 --> 17:05.622
She's an old friend
and I'm helping her out.

17:05.798 --> 17:09.359
You really wanna help her out?
Sneak up behind her with a big rock.

17:11.470 --> 17:14.371
- Detox?
- No. Constipated.

17:15.040 --> 17:16.667
Because you're detoxing?

17:17.543 --> 17:19.773
- Can we just do this?
- Fine.

17:22.014 --> 17:25.950
&lt;i>'Cause your mama was workin'
On the chain gang&lt;/i>

17:27.052 --> 17:28.110
&lt;i>Polk&lt;/i>

17:29.755 --> 17:30.813
&lt;i>Salad&lt;/i>

17:32.858 --> 17:34.689
That one felt really good.

17:34.860 --> 17:38.523
Okay, help me understand something.
You're hoping to bang her, right?

17:42.167 --> 17:44.135
Can I hear a little?

17:48.540 --> 17:50.804
Sure, play it back.

17:53.745 --> 17:55.713
&lt;i>Down in Louisiana&lt;/i>

17:57.082 --> 18:00.313
- That's me?
- That's you.

18:01.153 --> 18:02.814
Wow.

18:03.222 --> 18:05.656
I had no idea I was so good.

18:08.994 --> 18:12.430
Oh, Charlie, I'm so happy.

18:12.598 --> 18:16.193
Oh, well, if you're happy, I'm happy.

18:17.736 --> 18:22.332
- Why did I ever let you go?
- Lf I recall, you had a list of reasons.

18:22.507 --> 18:24.031
Well, I was wrong.

18:24.209 --> 18:25.540
How can I make it up to you?

18:25.711 --> 18:29.044
Uh, how do you wanna
make it up to me?

18:31.116 --> 18:32.413
Wow.

18:34.820 --> 18:36.048
There it is.

18:38.090 --> 18:41.821
Let's do this last track
and then we can go back to my place.

18:45.631 --> 18:48.122
Maybe we could sweeten her vocals
with some reverb...

18:48.333 --> 18:50.233
...a little echo, lay guitar over it.

18:50.402 --> 18:54.202
We could lay car horns
and barking dogs over it. Won't help.

18:57.476 --> 18:59.103
I'm ready.

18:59.645 --> 19:03.479
- Just relax and feel the groove, okay?
- I got it.

19:03.982 --> 19:08.749
Okay, this is "Boogie Woogie Bugle Boy,"
take one.

19:14.826 --> 19:17.522
&lt;i>He was a famous trumpet man
From out Chicago way&lt;/i>

19:17.696 --> 19:19.857
&lt;i>He had a boogie style
That no one else could play&lt;/i>

19:20.032 --> 19:22.330
&lt;i>Whoo, he was the top man at his craft&lt;/i>

19:22.501 --> 19:25.026
&lt;i>And then his number came up
And he was gone with the draft&lt;/i>

19:25.203 --> 19:27.671
&lt;i>He's in the Army now
Blowin' reveille&lt;/i>

19:27.839 --> 19:30.740
&lt;i>He's the boogie-woogie bugle boy
Of Company B&lt;/i>

19:30.909 --> 19:32.467
Okay, Mia, hold it a sec.

19:32.644 --> 19:36.307
- Is something wrong?
- Yeah, kind of.

19:36.481 --> 19:38.506
You can't sing.

19:38.684 --> 19:41.414
- What?
- You've got no talent.

19:41.586 --> 19:44.316
I'm sorry,
but we're both wasting our time here.

19:44.489 --> 19:48.789
I love Chelsea, I'm gonna marry her,
and I can't see you anymore.

19:48.961 --> 19:52.294
Are you kidding?
You can't just walk out on me, you...

19:54.333 --> 19:56.699
- Where's the bathroom?
- Down the hall.

19:56.902 --> 19:59.234
- Thanks.
- No, thank you.

20:02.207 --> 20:04.971
- Should have known this would happen,
you lowlife son of a bitch!

20:05.143 --> 20:07.111
The lowlife son of a bitch is gone...

20:07.279 --> 20:11.340
...but I think you have a real gift
and we should work together.

20:13.652 --> 20:16.280
Oh, you gotta be kidding me.

20:18.357 --> 20:20.917
Ah, you might wanna give it a minute.

20:22.194 --> 20:23.786
You were in there with your guitar?

20:23.962 --> 20:26.954
Well, you never know
when inspiration might strike.

20:33.672 --> 20:36.197
That's called
"Two Burritos and a Root Beer Float."

20:47.886 --> 20:50.252
Hey, how's the intestines?

20:50.689 --> 20:52.589
Clean as a whistle.

20:53.792 --> 20:55.760
It's the city's problem now.

21:01.266 --> 21:03.757
Yeah, ha, ha, very funny.

21:03.935 --> 21:07.302
What was in that so-called suppository
you gave me, anyway?

21:07.472 --> 21:10.999
Half a tab of Alka-Seltzer
crushed up in a gelcap.

21:11.977 --> 21:15.208
Oh. Well, that explains the foam.

21:16.648 --> 21:18.741
- I'm off to work.
- Have a good day, sweetie.

21:18.917 --> 21:20.509
- I'll be home around 6:30.
- Okay.

21:22.454 --> 21:24.149
- Alan?
- She's not living here.

21:24.322 --> 21:25.414
Just checking.

21:27.926 --> 21:30.451
And he calls me stupid.
